.TH QUANUXCTL-FOUNDRY 1 "February 2026" "QuanuX System Manual" "QuanuX Commands"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl-foundry \- The QuanuX generative AI engine for deterministic strategy compilation.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanuxctl" "foundry"
.I COMMAND
[
.I OPTIONS
]

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B foundry
module is the CLI interface to the QuanuX Generative AI Engine. It allows users to invoke LLMs to draft, verify, and vendor trading strategies across multiple languages (Python, Cython, C++) while enforcing mathematical equivalence via the Deterministic Sandbox.

Unlike standard code generation, the Foundry utilizes an intermediate JSON representation (IR) to define the logic AST before delegating language-specific bindings. This ensures zero drift between the backtested Python variant and the deployed C++ execution binary.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
.B forge
Initiates an AI generation pipeline to create a new sovereign component.
.br
\fBquanuxctl foundry forge --type <entry|exit|indicator|strategy> --name <Name> --lang <cpp|python|cython> [--version <string>]\fR
.br
Example: \fBquanuxctl foundry forge --type indicator --name OrderBookDelta --lang cpp --version 20\fR
.br
This command hits the REST API \fI/api/foundry/forge\fR, publishing the job to the NATS event bus.

.TP
.B verify
Triggers the Deterministic Sandbox against a generated strategy.
.br
\fBquanuxctl foundry verify --target <strategy_name>\fR
.br
The sandbox will isolate the compiled C++ code and the interpreted Python code, feed both engines an identical mock tick stream, and assert identical state variations. Code that drifts will fail verification.

.TP
.B deploy
Vendors the verified code components and pushes a self-sovereign artifact to an edge execution node.
.br
\fBquanuxctl foundry deploy --target <strategy_name> --node <remote_node_id>\fR

.TP
.B inspect
Connects to an edge node to allow real-time swapping of sovereign modules without halting the overarching execution loop.
.br
\fBquanuxctl foundry inspect <node_id>/<strategy>\fR

.SH ARCHITECTURE & NATS
Behind the scenes, the CLI interacts heavily with the NATS messaging topology:
.br
* \fBsys.foundry.request.forge\fR: Submits compilation jobs to the generator.
.br
* \fBsys.foundry.request.verify\fR: Submits test payloads to the sandbox.
.br
* \fBsys.foundry.stream.<job_id>\fR: Yields real-time generation tokens for UI streaming integration.

.SH FILES
.I server/foundry/schemas/*.json
- The mathematically binding Intermediate Representation (IR) schemas.
.br
.I server/foundry/engine/
- The Generator, Router, and Sandbox Python modules.
.br
.I server/foundry/entries/
- Generated files taxonomized by \fI<lang>/<version>/\fR.

.SH BUGS
Figma UI AI may incorrectly suggest "generic" trading components or assume standard C++ instead of the explicitly required C++20 standard. Always specify \fB--version 20\fR when issuing the C++ target language.

